s6-1-p3 = prose (cons "The following is the *typed Kripke schema* for normalization by evaluation. Write \(\mathsf{wk}:\Gamma\to\Gamma\mathbin{\triangleright}A\) for the weakening renaming; \(\mathsf{ren}_{r}\) for its action on neutrals and values; and \(\mathsf{neVar}_0\) for the newest neutral variable. A semantic function \(f:\mathsf{Val}(\Gamma,\Pi_{x:A}B)\) is natural under renamings and can be applied at an extended context. Its reification is" (cons "\[" (cons "\mathsf{reify}_{\Pi_{x:A}B}(f)" (cons " :=\mathsf{lam}\Bigl(" (cons " \mathsf{reify}_{B[\mathsf{var}_0/x]}" (cons " \bigl(\mathsf{appVal}(\mathsf{ren}_{\mathsf{wk}}f," (cons "       \mathsf{reflect}_{A}(\mathsf{neVar}_0))\bigr)\Bigr)." (cons "\]" (cons "For a neutral dependent function \(n\), reflection is the semantic function which, at any renaming \(r:\Gamma\to\Delta\) and value \(a:\mathsf{Val}(\Delta,A[r])\), returns" (cons "\[" (cons "\mathsf{reflect}_{B[r,\mathsf{reify}_{A[r]}(a)/x]}" (cons " \bigl(\mathsf{neApp}(\mathsf{ren}_r n," (cons "              \mathsf{reify}_{A[r]}(a))\bigr)." (cons "\]" (cons "For a dependent pair \(\Sigma_{x:A}B\), the neutral projections are indexed by the first component:" (cons "\[" (cons "\begin{aligned}" (cons "a&:=\mathsf{reflect}_A(\mathsf{neFst}(n)),\\" (cons "\mathsf{reflect}_{\Sigma_{x:A}B}(n)" (cons "&:=\bigl(a,\mathsf{reflect}_{B[a/x]}(\mathsf{neSnd}(n))\bigr),\\" (cons "\mathsf{reify}_{\Sigma_{x:A}B}(a,b)" (cons "&:=\bigl(\mathsf{reify}_A(a),\mathsf{reify}_{B[a/x]}(b)\bigr)." (cons "\end{aligned}" (cons "\]" (cons "For \(p:\mathsf{Val}(\Gamma,\mathsf{PathP}(A,a_0,a_1))\), reification is \(\mathsf{pathLam}(i.\mathsf{reify}_{A(i)}(\mathsf{pathApp}(p,i)))\); neutral reflection is the corresponding family \(i\mapsto\mathsf{reflect}_{A(i)}(\mathsf{nePathApp}(n,i))\), with the boundary equations \(i=0,1\) inherited from the path type. The full cubical semantic domain also interprets face restrictions, composition, and Glue using its specified Kan operations. These clauses describe the indicated fragment; their meaning is fixed by the chosen semantic model, rather than by an undefined universal quotation operation." nil)))))))))))))))))))))))))
